course: dictionary
lesson: 11866
title: Bookkeeping and keeping records
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are made from smaller words that help you guess. Bookkeeping is made from book and keeping. «Mum does the bookkeeping for her bakery every Sunday evening.» Keeping means looking after something, and a book is where things are written down, so she probably writes down the bakery's money.
explain: Read the rest of the sentence for more clues. A bakery spends money on flour and sugar, and it earns money from the cakes it sells. «Careful bookkeeping showed that the shop had made a profit this year.» Careful tells you the records were kept neatly and correctly, and profit is the money left over after costs are paid.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. Does «Mum does the record-keeping of money for her bakery» still make sense? Yes, so bookkeeping means keeping records of money.
fact: Bookkeeping means keeping careful written records of the money a business or person spends and earns.
fact: A person whose job is bookkeeping is called a bookkeeper.
fact: Bookkeeping can also mean keeping careful written records of anything, not just money.
fact: In maths and money lessons, bookkeeping helps you see the profit, which is the money left after costs are paid.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «do the bookkeeping» and «careful bookkeeping».
exercise: «Mum does the bookkeeping for her bakery every Sunday evening.» What does bookkeeping mean here? | *Keeping written records of the money the bakery spends and earns | Painting the signs above the shop door | Reading stories to the customers | Baking cakes and bread for the shop
exercise: Ella says a bookkeeper must read lots of books all day. What is a bookkeeper really? | Someone who reads stories aloud at school | Someone who delivers the post | Someone who sells books in a library | *Someone whose job is keeping records of money
exercise: What does «careful bookkeeping» suggest about a shop's records? | Lost in a pile on the floor | *Neat and correct | Very long and very boring | Written in pencil only
test: What does profit mean in «The shop's bookkeeping showed it made a profit»? | A new shop sign | The name of the owner | *Money left over after the costs are paid | A problem with the till
test: Which sentence uses bookkeeping correctly? | *Dad spent Saturday morning doing the bookkeeping for his small firm | The dog did the bookkeeping by barking at the postman | Bookkeeping is a loud green bird that sings at dawn | The bookkeeping ran across the field in the rain
exam: Which word could replace bookkeeping in «Careful bookkeeping kept the business safe» without changing the meaning? | Singing | Swimming | *Record-keeping | Gardening
